  "Id": 1652,
  "Title": "Professor Suria awarded Sitara-i-Imtiaz",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "The award is Pakistan's third highest civilian honour.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p>Professor Amin Suria has been awarded the prestigious Sitara-i-Imtiaz by the president of Pakistan. </p><p>One of the first faculty members to join the medical college in 1983, Dr Suria, a professor of pharmacology at AKU, is internationally recognised for his many scientific contributions most notably for elucidating the mechanisms of action of the benzodiazepine class of drugs.<br/></p>",
